  "basis": "Household calculations for 2029-30 (build fcfac709, policyengine-uk 2.177.7, certified in policyengine 6.20.2), on the OBR October 2026 forecast, with no survey data. Amounts are pounds a year. Each run is compared with current law for the same household.",
  "assumptions": [
    "Renters pay £6,000 a year (£500 a month) to a private landlord in the North West.",
    "Benefit rates, the minimum wage and tax thresholds are the engine's for 2029-30; every award is claimed in full, all year.",
    "The report's package is the health element removal and the PIP removal. The higher Youth Allowance and the employer National Insurance threshold are separate runs and are not added to the package's figure.",
    "The report's replacement payments (such as its additional cost allowance) are not modelled, so nothing is paid in place of the health element or PIP.",
    "Net income is after taxes and benefits and after a TV licence (£180 a year in the engine), before housing costs.",
    "Pay in the engine is 0.16% below hours times the hourly wage: its allowance for employers spreading the cost of the 2029 salary sacrifice cap across all pay.",
    "Hours, wages (other than the employer National Insurance saving paid as wages) and housing costs are held fixed; no behavioural response is modelled."
  ],
